I've been able to reproduce your issue in the latest version of Chrome (94.0.4606.81) and Firefox (92.0.1) on my end. The issue seems to be related to the `font-display` property of the font. 

When I set `font-display: swap` in the `@font-face` rule, the text appears correctly:

```css
@font-face {
  font-family: 'Noto Sans';
  src: url('/static/fonts/NotoSans-Regular.woff2') format('woff2');
  font-weight: 400;
  font-style: normal;
  font-display: swap;
}
```

Alternatively, you can use `font-display: fallback` which is similar to `swap` but with a shorter fallback period. I've tested this on your website and it seems to work
